# 🚨 Critical – Unapproved Application Connected to External Generative AI Service

**Severity:** 🔴 Critical  
**Platform:** 🔵 Microsoft Sentinel / Defender XDR  
**Data Source:** Microsoft Defender for Endpoint  
**Table:** `DeviceNetworkEvents`  
**Category:** 🟣 Shadow AI / AI Governance / Compliance  
**MITRE ATT&CK:** 🟠 T1071.001 – Web Protocols  

---

## 📌 Description

Detects non-browser applications, scripts, developer tools, or command-line utilities communicating with external Generative AI services such as OpenAI, Claude, Gemini, Copilot, GitHub Copilot, and Perplexity.

This may indicate unauthorized **Shadow AI usage** or potential exposure of organizational data.

---

## 🎯 Use Case

Identify applications communicating with external AI services outside the organization's approved application list.

Examples:

```text
python.exe      -> api.openai.com
powershell.exe  -> api.openai.com
node.exe        -> anthropic.com
curl.exe        -> api.openai.com
code.exe        -> claude.ai

---

##🔎 KQL Detection

let ApprovedProcesses = dynamic([
    "chrome.exe",
    "msedge.exe",
    "firefox.exe",
    "safari",
    "chatgpt",
    "copilot.exe",
    "outlook.exe",
    "msedgewebview2.exe"
]);

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where RemoteUrl has_any (
    "openai.com",
    "openai.azure.com",
    "copilot.microsoft.com",
    "claude.ai",
    "anthropic.com",
    "gemini.google.com",
    "perplexity.ai",
    "api.githubcopilot.com",
    "api.individual.githubcopilot.com"
)
| extend ProcName = tolower(InitiatingProcessFileName)
| where isnotempty(ProcName)
| where ProcName !in (ApprovedProcesses)
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceName,
    InitiatingProcessAccountName,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    RemoteUrl,
    RemoteIP,
    RemotePort
| order by Timestamp desc
